The tokens, skins, colour modes, headings and block styles moved to `content.css`, so the editor shows the content like the Public UI; `publicui.css` styles the frame in the `custom` layer, and nothing is unlayered. The brand color is `--brand`, and `--accent` is a subtle hover fill again. `@plone/layout` lays out the stack of blocks and applies the gutter and the room around the content. The title and the navigation align separately (`--align`, `--nav-align`): Default has a left aligned title and a centred navigation, Nieve aligns both left, Mercado centres both. A centred navigation is centred on the page, and the breadcrumbs' home icon sits on the text's centre line. Logging in and out are pills: logging in the primary action, logging out the secondary. In the Default skin, the quote is glass with the page's gradient, the callout has a brand tint (`--callout-background`), and teasers are glass cards, as in the first prototype. Sizes come from token scales: a spacing scale from `--space`, a type scale from `--font-size`, and line height, radius, tracking, control and icon size tokens, with every value rounded to a step. Responsive rules are container queries on the header, footer and content containers, and a centred navigation is a style query on `--nav-align`, which replaces the `--header-columns` token. The bundled Funnel fonts declare their weight range and an italic face, and the colour mode applies to the Public UI only, so the editor's content stays light. Full width blocks keep the page gutter in Default and Mercado (`--full-width-gutter: keep`, a style query) and run to the edges in Nieve. Teasers lift on hover by `--card-lift`: 2px in Default, 1px in Nieve and 4px in Mercado. Headings follow one ramp: each level from h6 (the body size) up is one half step of `--type-scale` above the next, h5 and h6 take the skin's heading style, and the room above a heading is 1.5 times its size. @danalvrz
